{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":850663,"ns":0,"title":"Trust (social science)","extract":"Trust is the belief that another person will do what is expected and is built through repeated consistency. It brings with it a willingness for one party (the trustor) to become vulnerable to another party (the trustee), on the presumption that the trustee will act in ways that benefit the trustor.","description":"Assumption of and reliance on the honesty of another party","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}